rules_rust fix: declare the x86_64-pc-windows-gnu triple.

`rust/platform/triple_mappings.bzl`: rules_rust deliberately omits the
*-windows-gnu triples because they map to the same Bazel constraints
(@platforms//os:windows + @platforms//cpu:x86_64) as *-windows-msvc, so a single
select cannot distinguish them. This repository builds only the gnu variant (the
Windows credential provider links with the hermetic zig cc_toolchain, no Visual
Studio), and its crate_universe lock lists only the gnu triple, so declaring it
is unambiguous here. Without the entry
`@rules_rust//rust/platform:x86_64-pc-windows-gnu` does not exist and every
generated crate select fails to resolve.

--- a/rust/platform/triple_mappings.bzl
+++ b/rust/platform/triple_mappings.bzl
@@ -44,6 +44,10 @@
 SUPPORTED_T2_PLATFORM_TRIPLES = {
     "aarch64-apple-ios": _support(std = True, host_tools = False),
     "aarch64-apple-ios-macabi": _support(std = True, host_tools = False),
+    # solutions/windows-logon-provider: only the gnu ABI is built, and only
+    # this triple appears in the crate_universe selects, so it does not clash
+    # with the msvc constraints.
+    "x86_64-pc-windows-gnu": _support(std = True, host_tools = False),
     "aarch64-apple-ios-sim": _support(std = True, host_tools = False),
     "aarch64-linux-android": _support(std = True, host_tools = False),
     "aarch64-pc-windows-msvc": _support(std = True, host_tools = True),
